abstract: >
  Scripts and results measuring how much the choice of sign catalogue moves
  the length-normalised conditional entropy of the rongorongo corpus (CEIPP,
  25 objects), a sweep over catalogue sizes, composition tests against the
  scribes' own substitutions, syllabary references (Rapa Nui, Maori, Linear B)
  at matched size and length, and transliteration-noise and Miller-Madow
  checks. Since 0.1 it also carries the Indus comparison on the same
  instrument, the calibrated decipherment attempt and its controls, the
  Mamari calendar anchor, the ligature correction to the repetition
  statistics, the genre and orthography controls in Hawaiian and Maori, and
  the per-sign ABAB audit. Standard-library Python; a fetch script downloads
  every input.
